  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Pedir con cortesía**",
      "",
      "- **Could you** + verbo base + *please*? → *Could you help me, please?* (¿podría ayudarme?)",
      "- **Could I** + verbo base…? → *Could I see your passport?* (¿podría ver…?)",
      "- **I'd like to** + verbo base → *I'd like to check in.* (quisiera…)",
      "- **Is / Are … included?** → *Is breakfast included?*",
      "",
      "**Responder:** *Of course. / Certainly. / Sure. / Sorry, I can't.* · Al entregar algo: *Here you are.*",
      "",
      "**Más frases útiles:** *What time is check-out?* · *Where is the lift?* · *Can I have the key, please?*",
      "",
      "Could es más educado que can. Después de could va el **verbo base** (sin to): *Could you help…* (no *Could you to help…*)."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "Could you to open the door?",
        "right": "Could you open the door?",
        "note": "Could no lleva to."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "I want a room.",
        "right": "I'd like a room, please.",
        "note": "I want suena demasiado directo."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
